---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — IG AutoDM">
<style>
.legal{padding:48px 0;max-width:800px}
.legal h1{font-size:36px;letter-spacing:-1px;margin-bottom:8px}
.legal .updated{font-size:13px;margin-bottom:32px}
.legal h2{font-size:22px;margin:32px 0 12px}
.legal p,.legal li{font-size:15px;margin-bottom:12px}
.legal ul{padding-left:24px}
</style>
<div class="legal"><div class="wrap">
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated muted">Last updated: September 2026</p>
<p>IG AutoDM (“we”, “the app”) automates Instagram comment replies and comment-triggered direct messages for creators and businesses who connect their own accounts.</p>
<h2>Data we collect</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Account data:</b> your login identity (via our auth provider) and the Instagram professional account and Facebook Page you choose to connect, including access tokens (stored encrypted).</li>
<li><b>Content data:</b> your posts/reels metadata, comments received on them, and the reply/DM configurations you create.</li>
<li><b>Log data:</b> records of automated replies and messages sent, skipped, or failed, with error reasons.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How we use it</h2>
<ul>
<li>To deliver the automation you configure (public comment replies and private replies via Meta's official Graph API).</li>
<li>To show you dashboards, logs, and account status.</li>
<li>We do <b>not</b> sell your data, show ads, or share data with third parties except Meta (to call their API on your behalf) and our infrastructure providers (hosting, database).</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data retention</h2>
<p>Tokens and configurations are kept while your account is connected. Logs are kept to operate and debug the service. Disconnecting your Instagram account stops all automation; see <a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a> to erase everything.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Request access, correction, or deletion of your data anytime via the contact below. Deletion requests are completed within 30 days.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Email: <a href="mailto:ligitg9@gmail.com">ligitg9@gmail.com</a></p>
</div></div>
</Base>
